        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>When a number ends in a zero, it&#x27;s easy to express that number in terms of tens. </p>",
            "readable_text": "When a number ends in a zero, it's easy to express that number in terms of tens.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, let&#x27;s consider the following number:</p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, let's consider the following number:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 15{\\color{blue}{0}}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 15{\\color{blue}{0}}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Notice that this number ends in a zero. Therefore, we can write it as a multiple of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10]</span> as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Notice that this number ends in a zero. Therefore, we can write it as a multiple of [MATH: 10] as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 15{\\color{blue}{0}} = 15 \\times 1{\\color{blue}{0}}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 15{\\color{blue}{0}} = 15 \\times 1{\\color{blue}{0}}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "graphic",
            "normalized_html": "<p><img src=\"/graphics/ad783d5a0dcd12dbfdd6862f07fb7eba\"></p>",
            "readable_text": "[IMG: /graphics/ad783d5a0dcd12dbfdd6862f07fb7eba]",
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "/graphics/ad783d5a0dcd12dbfdd6862f07fb7eba",
                "alt": ""
              }
            ],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Therefore, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 150]</span> is the same as &quot;<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 15]</span> tens.&quot;</p>",
            "readable_text": "Therefore, [MATH: 150] is the same as \"[MATH: 15] tens.\"",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>In the future, we&#x27;ll see how this method can be used to solve problems involving multiplication and division easily. </p>",
            "readable_text": "In the future, we'll see how this method can be used to solve problems involving multiplication and division easily.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [
          {
            "src": "/graphics/ad783d5a0dcd12dbfdd6862f07fb7eba",
            "alt": ""
          }
        ],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nWhen a number ends in a zero, it's easy to express that number in terms of tens.\n\nContent:\nFor example, let's consider the following number:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 15{\\color{blue}{0}}]\n\nContent:\nNotice that this number ends in a zero. Therefore, we can write it as a multiple of [MATH: 10] as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 15{\\color{blue}{0}} = 15 \\times 1{\\color{blue}{0}}]\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/ad783d5a0dcd12dbfdd6862f07fb7eba]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, [MATH: 150] is the same as \"[MATH: 15] tens.\"\n\nContent:\nIn the future, we'll see how this method can be used to solve problems involving multiplication and division easily."
      },
